      "text": "Computer architecture describes the interface between hardware and software. Understanding it explains why code has the performance characteristics it does — cache misses, branch misprediction, SIMD speedups, NUMA effects. You know the theory (Turing machines, von Neumann model, computability) — this guide is about what the silicon actually does in 2024."
